@startuml local-inference-scheduling-sequence
title Blaine — proposed local inference scheduling
skinparam shadowing false
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor<<proposed>> #FFF2CC

participant "Task A" as A
participant "Task B" as B
participant "Worker Selection" as Selection <<decision>>
participant "Local Inference Scheduler" as Scheduler <<proposed>>
participant "Inference Resource /\nResident Model" as Resource <<proposed>>

note over Selection,Scheduler
  Worker Selection decides WHAT MAY RUN.
  Scheduler decides WHEN / WHICH approved local candidate runs.
end note

== A. Reuse a sufficient resident candidate ==
A -> Selection : capability / quality requirement
Selection -> Scheduler : approved local candidate: resident
Scheduler -> Resource : allocate resident candidate
Resource --> Scheduler : execution complete
Scheduler --> A : run without model switch

== B. Prefer a sufficient resident choice ==
B -> Selection : requirement with several eligible choices
Selection -> Scheduler : approved candidates: resident, non-resident
Scheduler -> Resource : allocate sufficient resident candidate
Resource --> Scheduler : execution complete
Scheduler --> B : run; avoid unnecessary switch

== C. Wait, then switch only among eligible candidates ==
B -> Selection : requirement needs a different local candidate
Selection -> Scheduler : approved candidate: non-resident only
Scheduler -> Scheduler : queue while GPU is busy
Scheduler -> Resource : when free, switch and allocate approved candidate
Resource --> Scheduler : execution complete
Scheduler --> B : run after durable resource wait

== D. Residency never relaxes semantic requirements ==
A -> Selection : stricter capability / quality requirement
Selection --> A : resident candidate is insufficient; not approved
note over Selection,Scheduler
  No allocation occurs without an approved candidate.
  GPU contention does not automatically authorize paid cloud.
end note
@enduml
